// One way, down, and out.
//
// **The answer to the shelf-typing deadlock**, which `BALANCE.md`'s
// `storeroom` row has described since M2 and handed forward twice. A
// shelf takes whichever item lands on it first and holds only that
// until it empties, so a material arriving faster than it is consumed
// claims shelf after shelf until nothing else can be put down and the
// chain stops with the shelves apparently three-quarters full.
//
// A chute is the infrastructural answer rather than the settings-screen
// one (`SYSTEMS.md` §5.4): a thing you build, costing a slot column on
// every floor it spans like every other shaft, and what goes down it is
// gone. Surplus bamboo dumped is bamboo not milled later — the fix has
// an ongoing price, and you can *watch* the overflow leave, which puts
// the deadlock's cause on screen instead of leaving it to be inferred
// from a chain that quietly stopped.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
ShaftDef(
    id: "shaft.chute",
    name: "Chute",
    short: "CHU",
    kind: Chute,
    // **Poles alone, and that took finding out.**
    //
    // `SYSTEMS.md` §5.4 specified 6 poles and 2 rope, on the reasoning
    // that the rope stopped a chute being the trivially correct first
    // build. That reasoning is fine and the cost was wrong, which the
    // golden recorder demonstrated the first time it ran: the tower
    // jammed on shelves exactly as designed, and then could not build
    // the chute, because rope needs a ropery, and a ropery needs fiber
    // to reach it, and fiber has nowhere to go — which is the jam.
    //
    // **An escape hatch you can only afford before you need it is not an
    // escape hatch.** Everything else in the pack may be gated behind a
    // chain; this one may not, because it is the thing you reach for
    // when the chain has stopped. Six poles and a slot column on every
    // floor it spans is cost enough — and a tower that is not jammed
    // gains nothing at all from owning one.
    build_cost: [CostEntryDef(item: "item.poles", amount: 6)],
    // Reaches from anywhere down to the ground, so a spill gate is
    // always at the bottom of it.
    min_span: 2,
    max_span: 14,
    // Nothing rides a chute and nothing queues for one. Kept at the
    // schema minimum; neither field is read for this kind.
    capacity: 1,
    ticks_per_floor: 1,
    // Free. Things fall (`v2-plan.md` §6.2 — stairs, ladders and chutes
    // are the transports that cost no charge).
    charge_per_floor: 0,
    cars: 0,
    batch: 0,
)
